What in this repository is derived from it
------------------------------------------

Two datasets, in two modules. Both are DERIVED — filtered, reformatted and
re-keyed — rather than copied, which is use under the same terms rather than
outside them.

  kranji-core
    kranji/phonic/*.tsv          22 files, 8,100 characters, 8,763 readings.
                                 Built from the fields kTGHZ2013, kMandarin
                                 and kHanyuPinlu. Each file repeats this
                                 attribution in its own header.

  kranji-gloss-seed
    kranji/seed/pNNN.tsv         101 files, 7,146 seeded (character, reading)
    kranji/seed/pNNN.flags.tsv   glosses, built from the field kDefinition,
                                 plus the log of what could not be seeded
                                 cleanly.

The raw Unihan drop itself is NOT redistributed: it is read from input/ during
generation, and input/ is not tracked.

Everything else under kranji-gloss — the hand-written glosses and the phrases
that show them — is authored for this project and derives from no third-party
source. That separation is the reason kranji-gloss and kranji-gloss-seed are
different modules, and it is checkable from the dependency graph rather than
from this file.


